questions.stem:
A label printer joins one tag per level after the recursive call has returned, so the tail of the method stays non-tail. Fill the blank so tagList(new int[]{4, 7}, 0) returns "4|7".
static String tagList(int[] a, int i) {
  if (i >= a.length) return "";
  String rest = _____;
  if (rest.isEmpty()) return String.valueOf(a[i]);
  return a[i] + "|" + rest;
}

A developer wrote a recursive lister and claims it prints the bins in file order.
static void line(int[] a, int i) {
  if (i >= a.length) return;
  line(a, i + 1);
  System.out.print(a[i] + " ");
}
line(new int[]{3, 8, 5}, 0);
What does the program actually print?

A watchtower counts down by twos and must stop for every positive start, but odd starts never stop. The method is
static int parity(int n) {
  if (n % 2 == 0) return 0;
  return 1 + parity(n - 2);
}
Which base case makes the guard reachable for every positive start?

A committee is writing a binomial chooser and has already fixed the two stopping conditions, so only the value they return is in question. The method is
static int choose(int n, int k) {
  if (k == 0 || k == n) return 1;
  return choose(n - 1, k - 1) + choose(n - 1, k);
}
What integer does choose(6, 3) return?

A greenhouse walks its readings and treats 0 as an ordinary value, so the base case must stop only after the last index has been used. Fill the blank.
static int warm(int[] t, int i) {
  /* blank */
  return (t[i] > 0 ? 1 : 0) + warm(t, i + 1);
}

A quality desk counts crates over 100 kg but the run never finishes and eventually overflows the stack. The method is
static int over100(int[] a, int i) {
  if (i == a.length) return 0;
  return over100(a, i) + (a[i] > 100 ? 1 : 0);
}
Which statement identifies the fault?

A reviewer rejects this total because every level re-walks the rest of the array.
static int suffix(int[] a, int i) { if (i == a.length) return 0; return a[i] + suffix(a, i + 1); }
static int total(int[] a, int i) { if (i == a.length) return 0; return suffix(a, i) + total(a, i + 1); }
How many times does suffix read an element of the array while total runs on an array of 5 elements from index 0?

A report collects only the even readings into a comma joined string as it walks, so the accumulated text has to come back out. Fill the blank so evens(new int[]{3, 8, 5}, 0, "") returns "8".
static String evens(int[] a, int i, String soFar) {
  /* blank */
  if (a[i] % 2 == 0) return evens(a, i + 1, soFar.isEmpty() ? String.valueOf(a[i]) : soFar + "," + a[i]);
  return evens(a, i + 1, soFar);
}

A form checker must report false as soon as it meets a blank field, and the guard above already consumed position i. Fill the blank so a blank at index 1 ends the walk instead of being tested after the rest of the array.
static boolean noBlanks(String[] f, int i) {
  if (i == f.length) return true;
  if (f[i].isBlank()) return false;
  return _____;
}

A tile yard grows a pattern whose second value is fixed by rule rather than derived from the first. The method is
static int steps(int n) {
  if (n == 1) return 1;
  if (n == 2) return 3;
  return steps(n - 1) + steps(n - 2);
}
What integer does steps(5) return?

A survey tool counts adjacent pairs that rise, and a developer claims pairs(new int[]{1, 5, 2, 6}, 0) returns 3.
static int pairs(int[] a, int i) {
  if (i + 1 >= a.length) return 0;
  int rest = pairs(a, i + 1);
  if (a[i] < a[i + 1]) rest++;
  return rest;
}
Which claim about the value it actually returns is true?

A weather station asks for the smallest reading in slots 0 through 3 of {7, 2, 9, 4} but its helper reports 9.
static int minOf(int[] a, int lo, int hi) {
  if (lo == hi) return a[lo];
  int rest = minOf(a, lo + 1, hi);
  return Math.max(a[lo], rest);
}
Which statement identifies the fault?

Two helpers split one job: drop handles a water drop, burst handles a steam burst, and each hands off to the other with a smaller measure so the pair always ends. Fill the blank.
static int drop(int n) { if (n <= 0) return 0; return 1 + burst(n - 1); }
static int burst(int m) { if (m <= 0) return 0; return 1 + _____; }

A till tape stores its readings in an array whose last slot is the marker -999, and the total must stop there without reading past it. Fill the blank.
static int tapeTotal(int[] values, int i) {
  if (values[i] == -999) return 0;
  return values[i] + tapeTotal(_____);
}

A tracker keeps the best value while walking an array.
int best = a[0];
for (int i = 1; i < a.length; i++) { if (a[i] > best) best = a[i]; }
The loop is being rewritten as a recursive helper that keeps the same result. Fill the blank.
static int biggest(int[] a, int i) {
  if (i == a.length - 1) return a[i];
  return Math.max(a[i], biggest(a, _____));
}

A seating chart is walked one cell at a time by a helper that takes the width and the height, and it stops as soon as either measure runs out.
static int cells(int w, int h) {
  if (w == 0 || h == 0) return 0;
  return w + cells(w - 1, h);
}
What integer does cells(3, 4) return?

A serial number tool peels the last digit off a number and rebuilds the text after the call returns, so the digits come out in their original order. Fill the blank so serial(3051) returns "3051".
static String serial(int n) {
  if (n < 10) return String.valueOf(n);
  return _____ + (n % 10);
}

A tournament bracket is drawn recursively: an entry with one entrant is a leaf, and anything larger is split into two halves and adds one level.
static int depth(int entrants) {
  if (entrants <= 1) return 0;
  int half = entrants / 2;
  return 1 + Math.max(depth(half), depth(entrants - half));
}
What integer does depth(7) return?

A shelf helper is meant to report the first reading at or above 80 and to stop the moment it finds one. On {3, 90, 95} it does return the right index, but it keeps walking past the match. The method is
static int firstBig(int[] a, int i, int limit) {
  if (i == a.length) return -1;
  int rest = firstBig(a, i + 1, limit);
  return (a[i] >= limit) ? i : rest;
}
Which statement identifies what the written shape costs?

A stair helper solves the same smaller stair twice per level, and a writer wants to cache results so each distinct subproblem is solved once. The method is
static int climb(int n) {
  if (n <= 0) return 0;
  return 1 + climb(n - 1) + climb(n - 1);
}
How many distinct values of n does climb(4) reach, counting n = 4 itself?

A ledger helper sums a half open range, covering lo up to but not including hi, and a developer claims prefix(new int[]{2, 5, 1}, 0, 3) returns 3.
static int prefix(int[] a, int lo, int hi) {
  if (lo >= hi) return 0;
  return a[lo] + prefix(a, lo + 1, hi);
}
Which claim about the value it actually returns is true?

A formatter opens a marker at every level and closes them all at the end from one tail call, so the number of pending closers has to travel alongside the countdown. Fill the blank so marks(3, 0) prints exactly <<<>>>.
static void marks(int n, int closed) {
  if (n == 0) { for (int k = 0; k < closed; k++) System.out.print('>'); return; }
  System.out.print('<');
  marks(_____);
}

A guild reviews a written solution and accepts it only if it terminates and reports the right value. The method is
static int largest(int[] a, int i) {
  if (i == a.length) return Integer.MIN_VALUE;
  return Math.max(a[i], largest(a, i + 1));
}
Which claims about this written solution are true? Select all that apply.
